ral. Correct. CLEAN.\n\n0048: \"one of the bone giants stepped forward attempting to knock me down\" → \"其中一个骨巨人走上前来，试图把我打倒\" — correct. CLEAN.\n\n0049: \"as I attacked it, this bone giant would also rearrange its bones\" → \"在我攻击它的时候，这个骨巨人也会移动它的骨骼来强化自己\" — \"rearrange its bones\" → \"移动它的骨骼\" ok; \"来强化自己\" (to strengthen itself) is an addition. Material? It adds purpose not in source. Minor addition. Hmm. \"rearrange its bones\" → \"移动它的骨骼\" alone is odd; 强化自己 is inferable purpose. It's a reasonable translation of implied purpose. I'd say acceptable → CLEAN? Addition of purpose clause is inferable. I'll say CLEAN.\n\nHmm, actually \"rearrange its bones\" — 移动 (move) vs 重排 (rearrange). \"移动骨骼\" = move bones. Slightly loose but ok. 强化自己 addition — inferable. CLEAN.\n\n0050: \"I slowly leaned in, kissing him again\" → \"我慢慢俯身，再次亲吻他\" — 俯身 = bend down/lean over. Bounded: leaning in, not crouching. 俯身 is bending forward/leaning down — acceptable for leaning in to kiss. CLEAN.\n\n0051: source \"They possess no cultural identity or history to fall back on and sit on the precipice between the civilised races of Eyal's surface and the horrors of Eyal's underground.\" → target \"他们没有文化认同，也没有可供依凭的历史，处在埃亚尔地表的文明种族与地下的恐魔之间。\" — \"horrors\" → 恐魔 (horror creatures — in ToME, \"horror\" is translated 恐魔). Good. Precipice between — 处在...之间 fine (\"sit on the precipice\" rendered as 处在之间, dropping precipice metaphor but meaning kept). CLEAN.\n\nAlso drops \"Eyal's\" for underground: \"地下的恐魔\" vs \"Eyal's underground\" — 埃亚尔地表 vs 地下 — the second 埃亚尔 dropped, minor but same referent. CLEAN.\n\n0052: \"make there way towards the worms brain cluster and destroy it\" → \"将某一个人传送到蠕虫的大脑里，然后摧毁它的脑簇\" — \"make there way towards\" → \"将某一个人传送到\" (teleport a certain person into)? Source says \"make their way towards the worm's brain cluster\" — target says teleport someone into the worm's brain. This is likely a quest text where you send someone (an adventurer?) — bounded context: \"'destroy it'